The routine which teleports you is called tele(), in trap.c.  You could
either modify that routine, or modify allmain.c where it calls tele()
"if(Teleportation && !rn2(85)) tele();".  

I'm not sure that it's really worth doing though.  After all, using 
^T costs you food, but when teleportation happens randomly, it's "free".
So you could think of this as a free turn -- if you want it move 
(anywhere you like).  If you don't press ".".

